/// Where `send_player` and `send_players` send players. A key that isn't one of these is an error; it names a server or a group.
#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub struct NetworkSendOptions {
    /// A server, by its name in the network.
    pub server: Option<String>,
    /// A group: the hub picks the instance with room.
    pub group: Option<String>,
    /// How the hub picks the group's instance for this send: `least` (the fewest players) or `fill` (the fullest with room); the group's own when left out (`group.<name>.balance` in the hub's `hub.properties`, `least` unless its owner says).
    pub balance: Option<String>,
    /// What arrives with them, when `data` isn't given.
    pub data: Value,
    /// Seconds it may wait, when there's no instance with room yet (none is ready, all are full, the server is starting): the hub holds it, first come first served, tells whatever runs the servers that the group is wanted (its webhook), and sends them as soon as one has room. They stay where they are meanwhile. At most 600; it fails after that, saying why it waited.
    pub wait: Option<f64>,
    /// Called while it waits, each time its place in the queue changes (1 is next), or with `status` when a service placing the group's players holds them (`position` 0). Without it, each player waiting who's on this server sees their place, or the status, on their action bar.
    pub on_wait: Option<Function>,
}

